{"created": "2018-10-30T17:35:49.066877+00:00", "modified": "2020-01-24T19:25:41.441280+00:00", "id": 1473724, "conceptrecid": "1342657", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.1342657", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "metadata": {"title": "The OpenEar library of 3D models of the human temporal bone based on computed tomography and micro-slicing", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "publication_date": "2019-01-08", "description": "<p>The OpenEar Dataset provides a library consisting of eight three-dimensional models of the human temporal bone to enable surgical training including color data. Each dataset is based on a combination of multimodal imaging including Cone Beam Computed Tomography (CBCT) and micro-slicing. 3D reconstruction of micro-slicing images and subsequent registration to CBCT images allowed for relatively efficient multimodal segmentation of inner ear compartments, middle ear bones, tympanic membrane, relevant nerve structures, blood vessels and the temporal bone. Raw data from the experiment as well as voxel data and triangulated models from the segmentation are provided in full for use in surgical simulators or any other application which relies on high quality models of the human temporal bone.</p>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Sieber, Daniel Manuel", "affiliation": "MED-EL Elektromedizinische Geraete, Innsbruck, Austria", "orcid": "0000-0001-7126-9160"}, {"name": "Erfurt, Peter", "affiliation": "Medizinische Hochschule Hannover, Germany"}, {"name": "John, Samuel", "affiliation": "Hoersys GmbH, Hannover, Germany"}, {"name": "Ribeiro dos Santos, Gabriel", "affiliation": "MED-EL Elektromedizinische Geraete, Innsbruck, Austria"}, {"name": "Schurzig, Daniel", "affiliation": "MED-EL Elektromedizinische Geraete, Innsbruck, Austria"}, {"name": "S\u00f8rensen, Mads S\u00f8lvsten", "affiliation": "Rigshospitalet, University of Copenhagen, Denmark"}, {"name": "Lenarz, Thomas", "affiliation": "Medizinische Hochschule Hannover, Germany"}], "contributors": [{"name": "Sieber, Daniel Manuel", "affiliation": "MED-EL Elektromedizinische Geraete, Innsbruck, Austria", "type": "ContactPerson", "orcid": "0000-0001-7126-9160"}], "keywords": ["Anatomy", "Human Temporal Bone", "Multimodal Modeling", "Surgical Simulation", "Visible Ear Simulator", "Histology", "Micro Slicing", "Cone Beam Computed Tomography CBCT"], "related_identifiers": [{"identifier": "10.1038/sdata.2018.297", "relation": "isDocumentedBy", "scheme": "doi"}], "resource_type": {"title": "Dataset", "type": "dataset"}, "journal": {"issue": "180297", "title": "Scientific Data", "volume": "6"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "1342657"}}]}, "notes": "The article related and explanatory to this dataset is available Open Access at https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2018.297"}, "title": "The OpenEar library of 3D models of the human temporal bone based on computed tomography and micro-slicing", "links": {"self": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1473724", "self_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1473724", "preview_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1473724?preview=1", "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "self_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "self_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.1473724", "reserve_doi": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1473724/draft/pids/doi", "parent": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1342657", "parent_html": "https://zenodo.org/records/1342657", "parent_doi": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.1342657", "parent_doi_html": "https://zenodo.org/doi/10.5281/zenodo.1342657", "self_iiif_manifest": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1473724/manifest", "self_iiif_sequence": "https://zenodo.org/api/iiif/record:1473724/sequence/default", "files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1473724/files", "media_files": "https://zenodo.org/api/records/1473724/media-files", "archi